#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:12
msgid "AguaClara Flow Control and Measurement Technologies"
msgstr "Tecnologías de control y medición de caudal de AguaClara"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:14
msgid ""
"This section explores AguaClara's search for constant head in chemical "
"dosing. The term **constant head** means that the driving head of a system, "
":math:`\\Delta z` or :math:`\\Delta h`, does not change over time, even as "
"water flows through or out of the system. Constant head implies constant "
"flow, since the energy driving the flow does not change."
msgstr ""
"Esta sección explora la búsqueda de AguaClara de carga constante en la "
"dosificación química. El término **carga constante** significa que la cabeza"
" de impulso de un sistema, :math:`\\Delta z` o :math:`\\Delta h`, no cambia "
"con el tiempo, incluso cuando el agua fluye a través o fuera del sistema. "
"carga constante implica un flujo constante, ya que la energía que impulsa el"
" flujo no cambia."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:16
msgid ""
"The challenge of constant head in chemical dosing for water treatment plants"
" is not *just* providing one continuous flow of chemicals; it is also "
"varying that flow of chemicals as the flow rate through the plant changes, "
"so that the concentration of chemicals in the raw water stays the same."
msgstr ""
"El reto de carga constante en la dosificación de productos químicos para "
"tratamiento de agua plantas no es *solo* proporcionar un flujo continuo de "
"sustancias químicas; también se varía que el flujo de sustancias químicas a "
"medida que el caudal por la planta cambia, de modo que la concentración de "
"sustancias en la agua cruda se mantenga igual."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:18
msgid ""
"Before diving into the technologies, recall the purpose of the chemicals "
"that we are seeking to constantly **dose**, and why it is important to keep "
"a constant, specific dose. Also recall that ‘dose’ means ‘concentration of "
"chemical’ *in the water we are trying to treat*, not in the stock tanks of "
"the chemicals. `Coagulant "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coagulation_(water_treatment)>`_ like alum, "
"PAC, and some iron-based chemicals are used to turn small particles into "
"bigger particles, allowing them to be captured more easily. Waters with high"
" `turbidity <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turbidity>`_, indicative of a lot"
" of particles like clay and bacteria, require more coagulant to treat "
"effectively. Additionally, waters with a lot of `organic matter "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Organic_matter>`_ require significantly more "
"coagulant to treat. `Chlorine "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water_chlorination>`_ is used to disinfect "
"water that has already been fully treated. A proper and consistent chlorine "
"dose is required, as too low of a dose creates a risk of reintroduction of "
"pathogens in the distribution system and too high of a dose increases the "
"risk of carcinogenic `disinfection byproduct <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki"
"/Disinfection_by-product>`_ formation."
msgstr ""
"Antes de adentrarte en las tecnologías, recuerda el propósito de los "
"químicos que buscamos **dosificar** constantemente y por qué es importante "
"mantener una dosis constante y específica. También recuerda que 'dosis' "
"significa 'concentración de químicos' *en el agua que intentamos tratar*,"
" no en los tanques de stock de los químicos. `Coagulante "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coagulation_(water_treatment)>`_ como el "
"sulfato de aluminio, el PAC y algunos productos químicos basados en hierro se utilizan "
"para convertir partículas pequeñas en partículas más grandes, permitiendo "
"que se capturen más fácilmente. Las aguas con alto `turbidity "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turbidity>`_, indicativas de muchas "
"partículas como arcilla y bacterias, requieren más coagulante para tratarse "
"eficazmente. Además, las aguas con mucha `materia orgánica "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Organic_matter>`_ requieren mucho más "
"coagulante para tratarse. `Cloro "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water_chlorination>`_ se utiliza para "
"desinfectar agua que ya ha sido completamente tratada. Se requiere una dosis"
" adecuada y constante de cloro, ya que una dosis demasiado baja genera un "
"riesgo de reintroducción de patógenos en el sistema de distribución y una "
"dosis demasiado alta aumenta el riesgo de formación de `disinfection "
"byproduct <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disinfection_by-product>`_ "
"cancerígenas."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:20
msgid ""
"This section will often refer to the proportionality between flow :math:`Q` "
"and head :math:`\\Delta h` (recall that :math:`\\Delta h = h_L` after "
"applying the head loss trick) by using the ‘proportional to’ symbol, "
":math:`\\propto`. It is important to remember that it doesn’t necessarily "
"matter whether :math:`Q` or :math:`h_L` goes first, :math:`Q \\propto "
"\\sqrt{h_L}` is equivalent to saying that :math:`h_L \\propto Q^2`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:26
msgid "“Almost Linear” Flow Controller"
msgstr "Controlador de flujo \"casi lineal\""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:28
msgid ""
"This device consists of a bottle of chemical solution, called the **Constant"
" Head Tank** (CHT), a float valve to keep a solution in the CHT at a "
"constant water level, a flexible tube starting at the bottom of the CHT, and"
" many precisely placed and equally spaced holes in a pipes. The holes in the"
" pipe hold the other end of the tube that starts at the CHT. Chemical "
"solution, either coagulant or chlorine, is stored in a stock tank somewhere "
"above the CHT. A different tube connects the stock tank to the float valve "
"within the CHT."
msgstr ""
"Este dispositivo consiste en una botella de solución química, llamada "
"**carga constante Tanque** (CHT), un válvula de flotador para mantener una "
"solución en el CHT a un nivel del agua constante, un tubo flexible que "
"comienza en la parte inferior del CHT y muchos orificios colocados con "
"precisión y equidistantes en las tuberías. Los orificios en el tubo "
"sostienen el otro extremo del tubo que comienza en el CHT. La solución "
"química, ya sea coagulante o cloro, se almacena en un tanque de stock en "
"algún lugar por encima del CHT. Un tubo diferente conecta el tanque de stock"
" con el válvula de flotador dentro del CHT."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:30
msgid ""
"This flow controller provides a constant flow of chemical solution to the "
"water in the plant. When the end of the flexible tube is placed in a hole, "
"the elevation difference between the water level in the bottle and the hole "
"is set and does not change unless the tube is then placed in another hole. "
"Thus, a constant flow is provided while the end of the tube is not moved."
msgstr ""
"Este controlador de flujo proporciona un flujo constante de solución química"
" al agua de la planta. Cuando el extremo del tubo flexible se coloca en un "
"agujero, la diferencia de elevación entre el nivel del agua de la botella y "
"el agujero se establece y no cambia a menos que el tubo se coloque en otro "
"agujero. Así, se proporciona un flujo constante mientras el extremo del tubo"
" no se mueve."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:32
msgid ""
"As has been mentioned previously, the amount of chlorine and coagulant that "
"must be added to the raw water changes depending on the flow rate of the "
"plant; the change is necessary to keep the dose constant. More water flowing"
" through the plant means more chlorine is necessary to maintain the dose of "
"chlorine in the treated water. For coagulant, there are also other factors "
"aside from plant flow rate that impact the required dose, including the "
"turbidity and amount of organic matter in the water. The operator must be "
"able to change the dose of both coagulant and chlorine quickly and easily, "
"and they must be able to know the value of the new dose they set. The "
"“Almost Linear” Flow Controller accomplishes this by having a large number "
"of holes in the flow control pipe next to the CHT. This large number of "
"holes gives the operator many options for adjusting the dose, and let them "
"quickly change the flow of chemicals into the raw water by moving the end of"
" the flexible tube from one hole to another."
msgstr ""
"Como se ha mencionado anteriormente, la cantidad de cloro y coagulante que "
"debe añadirse al agua cruda cambia según el caudal de la planta; el cambio "
"es necesario para mantener la dosis constante. Más agua fluyendo por la "
"planta significa que es necesario más cloro para mantener la dosis de cloro "
"en el agua tratada. Para el coagulante, también hay otros factores además de"
" las caudal de la planta que afectan a la dosis requerida, incluyendo la "
"turbidez y la cantidad de materia orgánica en el agua. El operador debe ser "
"capaz de cambiar la dosis tanto de coagulante como de cloro de forma rápida "
"y sencilla, y debe saber el valor de la nueva dosis que establezca. El "
"controlador de flujo \"Casi Lineal\" lo logra teniendo un gran número de "
"orificios en la tubería de control de flujo junto al CHT. Este gran número "
"de orificios ofrece al operador muchas opciones para ajustar la dosis, y les"
" permite cambiar rápidamente el flujo de productos químicos hacia el agua "
"cruda moviendo el extremo del tubo flexible de un orificio a otro."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:34
msgid ""
"The idea behind this flow controller is to have a linear relationship "
"between :math:`Q` and :math:`h_L` (remember that :math:`h_L` is equal to "
":math:`\\Delta h` when we apply the head loss trick), which can be written "
"as :math:`Q \\propto h_L`. Here, :math:`Q` is the flow of chemicals out of "
"the flexible tube, and :math:`h_L` is the elevation difference between the "
"water level in the CHT and the end of the flexible tube."
msgstr ""
"La idea detrás de este controlador de flujo es tener una relación lineal "
"entre :math:`Q` y :math:`h_L` (recuerda que :math:`h_L` es igual a "
":math:`\\Delta h` cuando aplicamos el truco pérdida de carga ), que puede "
"escribirse como :math:`Q \\propto h_L`. Aquí, :math:`Q` es el flujo de "
"productos químicos que salen del tubo flexible, y :math:`h_L` es la "
"diferencia de elevación entre el nivel del agua en el CHT y el extremo del "
"tubo flexible."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:36
msgid ""
"As you remember from section 1.5, the summary of Fluids Review, :math:`Q "
"\\propto \\Delta h`, or :math:`\\Delta h \\propto Q` as it was written in "
"the section summary, is only true for the combination of major losses and "
"laminar flow, which makes applicable the Hagen-Poiseuille equation. "
"Therefore, the flow must always be laminar in the flexible tube that goes "
"between the CHT and the holes, and major losses must far exceed minor "
"losses."
msgstr ""
"Como recorda de la sección 1.5, el resumen de Revisión de Fluidos, :math:`Q "
"\\propto \\Delta h`, o :math:`\\Delta h \\propto Q` como se escribió en el "
"resumen de la sección, solo es cierto para la combinación de pérdidas "
"mayores y flujo laminar, lo que hace aplicable la ecuación de Hagen-"
"Poiseuille. Por tanto, el flujo debe ser siempre laminar en el tubo flexible"
" que va entre el CHT y los agujeros, y las pérdidas mayores deben superar "
"con creces las pérdidas menores."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:38
msgid ""
"It is easy to design for laminar flow, but the “Almost Linear” Flow "
"Controller was unable to make major losses far exceed minor losses. The "
"bending in the flexible tube caused a lot of minor losses which changed in "
"magnitude depending on exactly how the tube was bent. This made the flow "
"controller “almost linear,” but that wasn’t good enough."
msgstr ""
"Es fácil de diseñar para flujo laminar, pero el controlador de flujo \"casi "
"lineal\" no pudo hacer que las pérdidas mayores superaran con creces las "
"menores. La curvatura del tubo flexible causaba muchas pérdidas menores que "
"cambiaban de magnitud según cómo se doblaba exactamente el tubo. Esto hacía "
"que el controlador de flujo fuera \"casi lineal\", pero eso no era "
"suficiente."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:40
msgid "Notes:"
msgstr "Notas:"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:42
msgid "This flow controller is **no longer used by AguaClara.**"
msgstr "Este controlador de flujo **ya no es utilizado por AguaClara.**"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:43
msgid ""
"The tube connecting the CHT to the outlet of chemicals must be very long "
"and, more importantly, **straight** to form a linear relationship between "
"driving head and flow. This linear relationship was not true for the “Almost"
" Linear” Flow Controller, and is why it was replaced by the Linear Chemical "
"Dose Controller (CDC). The CDC will be covered in more depth later on in "
"this section."
msgstr ""
"El tubo que conecta el CHT con la salida de productos químicos debe ser muy "
"largo y, más importante aún, **recto** para formar una relación lineal entre"
" la cabeza de impulso y el flujo. Esta relación lineal no era cierta para el"
" Controlador de Flujo \"Casi Lineal\", y por eso fue reemplazado por el "
"Controlador de Dosis Química Lineal (CDC). El CDC se explicará con más "
"profundidad más adelante en esta sección."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:49
msgid "Linear Flow Orifice Meter (LFOM)"
msgstr "Medidor de orificio de flujo lineal (LFOM)"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:51
msgid ""
"The LFOM is a weir shape cut into a pipe. It was meant to imitate `the Sutro"
" Weir "
"<https://confluence.cornell.edu/display/AGUACLARA/LFOM+sutro+weir+research>`_"
" while being far easier to build. The LFOM is a pipe with rows of holes, or "
"orifices, drilled into it. There are progressively fewer holes per row as "
"you move up the LFOM, as the shape is meant to resemble half a parabola on "
"each side. The size of all holes is the same, and the amount of holes per "
"row are precisely calculated. Water in the entrance tank flows into and down"
" the LFOM, towards the rapid mix orifice and flocculator."
msgstr ""
"El LFOM es una forma de vertedero cortada en una tubería. Estaba diseñado "
"para imitar `the Sutro Weir "
"<https://confluence.cornell.edu/display/AGUACLARA/LFOM+sutro+weir+research>`_"
" y ser mucho más fácil de construir. El LFOM es una tubería con filas de "
"agujeros, u orificios, perforados en ella. A medida que avanzas por el LFOM,"
" hay progresivamente menos agujeros por fila, ya que la forma está pensada "
"para parecerse a media parábola en cada lado. El tamaño de todos los "
"agujeros es el mismo y la cantidad de agujeros por fila se calcula con "
"precisión. El agua en el tanque de entrada fluye hacia el LFOM y hacia "
"abajo, hacia el mezcla rápida orificio y el floculador."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:60
msgid "A sutro weir and an LFOM"
msgstr "Un vertedero Sutro y un LFOM"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:60
msgid ""
"On the left is a sutro weir. On the right is AguaClara's approximation of "
"the sutro weir's geometery. This elegant innovation is called a linear flow "
"orifice meter, or LFOM for short."
msgstr ""
"A la izquierda hay un vertedero Sutro. A la derecha está la aproximación de "
"AguaClara a la geometría del vertedero Sutro. Esta elegante innovación se "
"denomina medidor de orificio lineal de flujo, o LFOM por sus siglas en "
"inglés."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:62
msgid "The LFOM does one thing and serves two purposes."
msgstr "El LFOM hace una cosa y cumple dos propósitos."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:64
msgid "What it does:"
msgstr "Qué hace:"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:66
msgid ""
"**The LFOM creates a linear relationship between water level in the entrance"
" tank and the flow out of the entrance tank.** *It does not control the flow"
" through the plant*. If the LFOM were replaced with a hole in the bottom of "
"the entrance tank, the same flow rate would go through the plant, the only "
"difference being that the water level in the entrance tank would scale with "
"flow squared :math:`h \\propto Q^2` instead of :math:`h \\propto Q`. For "
"example, if an LFOM has 10 rows of holes and has been designed for a plant "
"whose maximum flow rate is 10 L/s, then the operator knows that the number "
"of rows submerged in water is equal to the flow rate of the plant in L/s. So"
" if the water were up to the third row of holes, there would be 3 L/s of "
"water flowing through the plant."
msgstr ""
"**El LFOM crea una relación lineal entre nivel del agua en el tanque de "
"entrada y el flujo que sale del tanque de entrada.** *No controla el flujo a"
" través de la planta*. Si el LFOM se reemplazara por un agujero en el fondo "
"del tanque de entrada, el mismo caudal atravesaría la planta, la única "
"diferencia es que el nivel del agua en el tanque de entrada escalaría con el"
" flujo al cuadrado :math:`h \\propto Q^2` en lugar de :math:`h \\propto Q`. "
"Por ejemplo, si un LFOM tiene 10 filas de agujeros y ha sido diseñado para "
"una planta cuyo caudal máximo es de 10 L/s, entonces el operador sabe que el"
" número de hileras sumergidas en agua es igual al caudal de la planta en "
"L/s. Así que si el agua llegara hasta la tercera fila de agujeros, habría 3 "
"L/s de agua fluyendo por la planta."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:68
msgid "Why it is useful:"
msgstr "Por qué es útil:"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:70
msgid ""
"Allows the operator to measure the flow through the plant quickly and "
"easily, explained above."
msgstr ""
"Permite al operador medir el caudal a través de la planta de forma rápida y "
"sencilla, como se explicó anteriormente."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:71
msgid ""
"Allows for the Linear Chemical Dose Controller, which will be explained "
"next, to automatically adjust the flow of coagulant/chlorine into the plant "
"as the plant flow rate changes. This means the operator would only need to "
"adjust the flow of coagulant when there is a change in turbidity or organic "
"matter."
msgstr ""
"Permite que el Controlador Lineal de Dosis Química, que se explicará a "
"continuación, ajuste automáticamente el flujo de coagulante/cloro hacia la "
"planta a medida que la planta caudal cambia. Esto significa que el operador "
"solo tendría que ajustar el flujo de coagulante cuando haya un cambio en la "
"turbidez o en materia orgánica."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:73
msgid ""
"This is best understood with examples. By shaping a weir differently, "
"different relationships between :math:`Q` and :math:`h` are formed: * In the"
" case of a `rectangular weir "
"<https://swmm5.files.wordpress.com/2016/09/image00124.jpg>`_, :math:`Q "
"\\propto h^{\\frac{3}{2}}` * In the case of a `v-notch weir "
"<https://swmm5.files.wordpress.com/2016/09/image0096.jpg>`_, :math:`Q "
"\\propto h^{\\frac{5}{2}}` * In the case of a `Sutro weir "
"<http://www.engineeringexcelspreadsheets.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/11"
"/Sutro-Weir-Diagram1.jpg>`_ and thus LFOM, :math:`Q \\propto h`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:79
msgid ""
"Before the water level reaches the second row of holes, the LFOM is "
"simulating a rectangular weir, and thus :math:`h \\not\\propto Q`. The Sutro"
" weir also experiences this problem. Similarly, if the water level exceeds "
"the topmost row of the LFOM’s orifices, the linearity also breaks down. The "
"entire LFOM begins to act like an orifice, the exponent of :math:`Q` in "
":math:`h \\propto Q` becomes greater than 1. This is because the LFOM "
"approaches orifice behavior, and for orifices, :math:`h \\propto Q^2`."
msgstr ""
"Antes de que el nivel del agua llegue a la segunda fila de agujeros, el LFOM"
" simula un vertedero rectangular y, por tanto, :math:`h \\not\\propto Q`. El "
"vertedero Sutro también experimenta este problema. De manera similar, si el nivel del"
" agua excede la fila superior de los orificios del LFOM, la linealidad "
"también se rompe. Todo el LFOM comienza a actuar como un orificio, el "
"exponente de :math:`Q` en :math:`h \\propto Q` se vuelve mayor que 1. Esto "
"se debe a que el LFOM se aproxima al comportamiento del orificio, y para los"
" orificios, :math:`h \\propto Q^2`."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:81
msgid ""
"The diameter of the LFOM pipe is set by the velocity of the falling water "
"inside the LFOM at the bottom of the bottom row of orifices. This velocity "
"is obtained by summing up all of the momentum of the falling water and "
"dividing by the total flow for the case where the LFOM is operating at "
"maximum capacity. The Sutro weir equations (not yet provided here) can be "
"integrated to obtain an equation for the falling velocity of the water "
"inside the LFOM. This maximum vertical velocity of the falling water sets "
"the minimum flow area of the LFOM and hence continuity can be used to obtain"
" the minimum pipe diameter."
msgstr ""
"El diámetro de la tubería del LFOM se determina por la velocidad del agua "
"que cae dentro del LFOM en la parte inferior de la fila inferior de "
"orificios. Esta velocidad se obtiene sumando todo el momento del agua que "
"cae y dividiendo por el flujo total para el caso en que el LFOM esté "
"funcionando a máxima capacidad. Las ecuaciones del vertedero Sutro (aún no "
"proporcionadas aquí) pueden integrarse para obtener una ecuación para la "
"velocidad de caída del agua dentro del LFOM. Esta velocidad vertical máxima "
"del agua descendente establece el área mínima de flujo del LFOM y, por "
"tanto, la continuidad puede usarse para obtener el diámetro mínimo de la "
"tubería."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:83
msgid "  V_{max} = \\frac{4}{3 \\pi} \\sqrt{2gh_L}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:93
msgid "Linear Chemical Dose Controller (CDC)"
msgstr "Controlador lineal de dosis química (CDC)"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:94
msgid ""
"Since the Linear Chemical Dose Controller has become the AguaClara standard "
"chemical dosing system, it is often simply called the Chemical Dose "
"Controller, **or CDC for short** (see :numref:`figure_cdc_and_lfom_in_et`)."
msgstr ""
"Dado que el Controlador de Dosis Química Lineal se ha convertido en el "
"estándar de AguaClara sistema de dosificación de químicos, a menudo se le "
"llama simplemente Controlador de Dosis Química, **o CDC para abreviar** "
"(véase :numref:`figure_cdc_and_lfom_in_et`)."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:103
msgid "A chemical dose controller and an LFOM"
msgstr "Un controlador de dosis química y un LFOM"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:103
msgid ""
"The LFOM and chemical dose controller work together to control the flow of "
"the chemicals."
msgstr ""
"El LFOM y el controlador de dosis química trabajan juntos para controlar el "
"flujo de los productos químicos."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:106
msgid ""
"The CDC brings together the LFOM and many improvements to the “Almost "
"Linear” Flow Controller. Let’s break it down, with the image below as a "
"guide."
msgstr ""
"El CDC reúne el LFOM y muchas mejoras del Controlador de Flujo \"Casi "
"Lineal\". Vamos a desglosarlo, con la imagen de abajo como guía."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:108
msgid ""
"Start at the Constant Head Tank (CHT). This is the same set up as the "
"“Almost Linear” Flow Controller. The stock tank feeds into the CHT, and the "
"float valve makes sure that the water level in the constant head tank is "
"always the same."
msgstr ""
"Empieza en el tanque carga constante (CHT). Esta es la misma configuración "
"que el controlador de flujo \"Casi Lineal\". El tanque de stock alimenta el "
"CHT, y el válvula de flotador se asegura de que la nivel del agua en el "
"tanque carga constante sea siempre la misma."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:110
msgid ""
"Now the tubes. These fix the linearity problems that were the main problem "
"in the “Almost Linear” Flow Controller."
msgstr ""
"Ahora los tubos. Estos solucionan los problemas de linealidad que eran el "
"principal problema en el controlador de flujo \"Casi Lineal\"."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:112
msgid ""
"The tube connected to the bottom of the CHT is large diameter to minimize "
"any head loss through it."
msgstr ""
"El tubo conectado a la parte inferior del CHT tiene un diámetro grande para "
"minimizar cualquier pérdida de carga a través de él."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:114
msgid ""
"The three thin, straight tubes are designed to generate a lot of major "
"losses and to minimize any minor losses. This is to make sure that major "
"losses far exceed any minor losses, which will ensure that the Hagen-"
"Poiseuille equation is applicable and that flow will be directly "
"proportional to the head, :math:`Q \\propto \\Delta h`. Why are there 3 "
"tubes?"
msgstr ""
"Los tres tubos delgados y rectos están diseñados para generar muchas "
"pérdidas importantes y minimizar cualquier pérdida menor. Esto es para "
"asegurarse de que las pérdidas mayores superen con creces cualquier pérdida "
"menor, lo que garantizará que la ecuación de Hagen-Poiseuille sea aplicable "
"y que el flujo sea directamente proporcional a la carga, :math:`Q \\propto "
"\\Delta h`. ¿Por qué hay 3 tubos?"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:116
msgid ""
"**3 short instead of 1 short** Removing 2 of the 3 tubes would mean 3 times "
"the flow through the remaining tube. This means the velocity in the tube "
"would be 3 times as fast. Since minor losses scale with :math:`v^2` and "
"major losses only scale with :math:`v`, this would increase the ratio of "
":math:`\\rm{\\frac{minor \\, losses}{major \\, losses}}`, which would break "
"the linearity we’re trying to achieve. It would also increase the total head"
" loss through the system, resulting in a lower maximum flow rate than "
"before."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:118
msgid ""
"**1 long instead of 3 short** One tube whose length is equal to the three "
"combined would be inconveniently long, and would suffer from the same "
"problems as above. There would be even more head loss through the tube, "
"since its length would be longer."
msgstr ""
"**1 largo en lugar de 3 corto** Un tubo cuya longitud sea igual a los tres "
"combinados sería incómodamente largo y sufriría los mismos problemas que "
"antes. Habría aún más pérdida de carga a través del tubo, ya que su longitud"
" sería mayor."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:120
msgid ""
"The large-diameter tube on the right of the three thin, straight tubes is "
"where the chemicals flow out. The end of the tube is connected to both a "
"slider and a ‘drop tube.’ The drop tube allows for supercritical flow of the"
" chemical leaving the dosing tubes; once the chemical enters the drop tube "
"it falls freely and no longer affects the CDC system."
msgstr ""
"El tubo de gran diámetro a la derecha de los tres tubos delgados y rectos es"
" donde salen los productos químicos. El extremo del tubo está conectado "
"tanto a un deslizador como a un 'tubo de caída'. El tubo de caída permite un"
" flujo supercrítico del químico que sale de los tubos de dosificación; una "
"vez que el químico entra en el tubo de caída, cae libremente y ya no afecta "
"al sistema CDC."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:122
msgid ""
"The slider rests on a lever. This lever is the critical part of the CDC, it "
"connects the water level in the entrance tank, which is adjusted by the "
"LFOM, to the difference in head between the CHT and the end of the dosing "
"tube. This allows the flow of chemicals to automatically adjust to a change "
"in the plant flow rate, maintaining a constant dose in the plant water. One "
"end of the lever tracks the water level in the entrance tank by using a "
"float. The counterweight on the other side of the lever is to make sure the "
"float ‘floats,’ since this float is usually made of PVC, which is more dense"
" than water."
msgstr ""
"El deslizador descansa sobre una palanca. Esta palanca es la parte crítica "
"del CDC, conecta la nivel del agua en el tanque de entrada, que es ajustada "
"por el LFOM, con la diferencia de altura entre el CHT y el extremo del tubo "
"dosificador. Esto permite que el flujo de productos químicos se ajuste "
"automáticamente a un cambio en el caudal de la planta , manteniendo una "
"dosis constante en el agua de la planta. Un extremo de la palanca sigue el "
"nivel del agua en el tanque de entrada usando un flotador. El contrapeso en "
"el otro lado de la palanca es para asegurarse de que el flotador 'flote', ya"
" que este flotador suele estar hecho de PVC, que es más denso que el agua."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:124
msgid ""
"The slider itself controls the dose of chemicals. For any given plant flow "
"rate, the slider can be adjusted to increase or decrease the amount of "
"chemical flowing through the plant."
msgstr ""
"El propio deslizador controla la dosis de productos químicos. Para cualquier"
" caudal de planta dado, el deslizador puede ajustarse para aumentar o "
"disminuir la cantidad de sustancia química que circula por la planta."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:133
msgid "CDC Displayed"
msgstr "CDC Mostrado"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:133
msgid "This is the setup of the chemical dose controller."
msgstr "Esta es la configuración del controlador de dosis química."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:135
msgid ""
"The CDC makes it easy and accurate to dose chemicals. The flow of chemicals "
"automatically adjusts to changes in the plant flow rate to keep a constant "
"dose, set by the operator. When a turbidity event occurs, the operator can "
"change the dose of coagulant by moving the coagulant slider *lower* on the "
"lever to increase the dose. The slider has labelled marks so the operator "
"can record the dose accurately."
msgstr ""
"El CDC facilita y precisa la dosificación de productos químicos. El flujo de"
" productos químicos se ajusta automáticamente a los cambios en la planta "
"caudal para mantener una dosis constante, establecida por el operador. "
"Cuando ocurre un evento de turbidez, el operador puede cambiar la dosis de "
"coagulante moviendo la deslizador de coagulante *más abajo* en la palanca "
"para aumentar la dosis. El deslizador tiene marcas etiquetadas para que el "
"operador pueda registrar la dosis con precisión."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:137
msgid ""
"A lot of design has gone into the CDC. The design equations and their "
"derivations that the following steps are based on can be found here: "
":ref:`heading_design_equations_for_the_cdc`, and you are very, very strongly"
" encouraged to read them."
msgstr ""
"Mucho diseño ha entrado en el CDC. Las ecuaciones de diseño y sus "
"derivaciones en las que se basan los siguientes pasos se pueden encontrar "
"aquí: :ref:`heading_design_equations_for_the_cdc`, y se te anima muchísimo a"
" leerlas."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:139
msgid ""
"The CDC can be designed manually using the equations from the derivation "
"linked above or via aguaclara, using the equations found in "
"`cdc_functions.py <https://github.com/AguaClara/aguaclara>`_. Either way, "
"the design algorithm is roughly the same:"
msgstr ""
"El CDC puede diseñarse manualmente usando las ecuaciones de la derivación "
"enlazada arriba o mediante aguaclara, usando las ecuaciones encontradas en "
"`cdc_functions.py <https://github.com/AguaClara/aguaclara>`_. En cualquier "
"caso, el algoritmo de diseño es aproximadamente el mismo:"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:141
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Calculate the maximum flow rate, :math:`Q_{max, \\, Tube}`, through each "
"available dosing tube diameter :math:`D` that keeps error due to minor "
"losses below 10% of total head loss. Recall that tubing diameter is an "
"array, as there are many diameters available at hardware stores and "
"suppliers. This means that for each step, there will be as many solutions as"
" there are reasonable diameters available."
msgstr ""
"Calcula el máximo caudal, :math:`Q_{max, \\, Tube}`, a través de cada "
"diámetro disponible del tubo de dosificación :math:`D` que mantenga el error"
" debido a pérdidas menores por debajo del 10% del total de pérdida de carga."
" Recuerda que el diámetro del tubo es un conjunto, ya que hay muchos "
"diámetros disponibles en ferreterías y proveedores. Esto significa que para "
"cada paso habrá tantas soluciones como diámetros razonables disponibles."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:143
msgid ""
"  Q_{max, \\, Tube} = \\frac{\\pi D^2}{4} \\sqrt{\\frac{2 h_L g "
"\\Pi_{Error}}{\\sum{K} }}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:148
msgid ""
"Calculate how much flow of chemical needs to pass through the CDC at maximum"
" plant flow and maximum chemical dose. This depends on the concentration of "
"chemicals in the stock tank."
msgstr ""
"Calcula cuánto flujo de producto químico debe pasar por el CDC al máximo "
"caudal de la planta y a la dosis máxima de químico. Esto depende de la "
"concentración de productos químicos en el tanque de stock."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:150
msgid "Q_{max, \\, CDC} = \\frac{Q_{Plant} \\cdot C_{Dose, \\, max}}{C_{StockTank}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:154
msgid ""
"Calculate the number of dosing tubes required if the tubes flow at  maximum "
"capacity (round up)"
msgstr ""
"Calcular el número de tubos de dosificación necesarios si los tubos fluyen a"
" máxima capacidad (redondeando hacia arriba)"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:156
msgid ""
"n_{Tubes} = {\\rm ceil} \\left( \\frac{Q_{max, \\, CDC}}{Q_{max, \\, Tube}} "
"\\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:160
msgid ""
"Calculate the length of dosing tube(s) that correspond to each available "
"tube diameter."
msgstr ""
"Calcula la longitud del(los) tubo(s) dosificador(es) que corresponden a cada"
" diámetro disponible."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:162
msgid ""
"L_{min} = \\left( \\frac{g h_L \\pi D^4}{128 \\nu Q_{max}} - "
"\\frac{Q_{max}}{16 \\pi \\nu} \\sum{K} \\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:166
msgid ""
"Select a tube length from your array of solutions. Pick the longest dosing "
"tube that you can, keeping in mind that the tube(s) must be able to fit in "
"the plant and can’t be longer than the length of the plant wall it will be "
"placed along."
msgstr ""
"Selecciona la longitud de un tubo de tus soluciones. Elige el tubo de "
"dosificación más largo que puedas, teniendo en cuenta que el/los tubo deben "
"poder encajar en la planta y no pueden ser más largos que la longitud de la "
"pared de la planta donde se colocará."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:168
msgid ""
"Finally, select the dosing tube diameter and flow rate corresponding to the "
"selected tube length."
msgstr ""
"Finalmente, selecciona el diámetro y el caudal del tubo dosificador "
"correspondientes a la longitud del tubo seleccionado."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:173
msgid "Chemical Feed Stock Concentrations"
msgstr "Concentraciones de materias primas químicas"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:175
msgid ""
"The AguaClara plants in Honduras have used chlorine stock concentrations "
"between 9 and 11 g/L of calcium hypochlorite. The stainless steel cotter pin"
" in the float valve only lasts about 4 months when the stock concentration "
"is 11 g/L. Thus a maximum calcium hypochlorite concentration of 9 g/L is "
"recommended. A supply of stainless steel cotter pins should be maintained at"
" each plant or a chlorine and acid resistant replacement should be "
"developed. Given the low cost of the stainless steel cotter pins it is "
"likely most cost effective to simply put those pins on a regular replacement"
" schedule. A PVC pin could be used, but PVC is weak in comparison with "
"stainless steel. A larger pin diameter would be needed and could be used by "
"enlarging the hole in the valve. Unfortunately there isn't much material "
"available in the float valve to allow a significant increase in pin "
"diameter."
msgstr ""
"Las plantas de AguaClara en Honduras han utilizado concentraciones de cloro "
"entre 9 y 11 g/L de hipoclorito de calcio. El pasador de acero inoxidable en"
" el válvula de flotador solo dura unos 4 meses cuando la concentración "
"original es de 11 g/L. Por tanto, se recomienda una concentración máxima de "
"hipoclorito de calcio de 9 g/L. En cada planta se debe mantener un "
"suministro de pasadores de acero inoxidable o desarrollar un reemplazo "
"resistente al cloro y al ácido. Dado el bajo coste de los pasadores de acero"
" inoxidable, probablemente sea más rentable simplemente sustituirlos con un "
"calendario regular de reemplazo. Se podría usar un pasador de PVC, pero el "
"PVC es débil en comparación con el acero inoxidable. Se necesitaría un "
"diámetro de pasador mayor que podría usarse ampliando el orificio de la "
"válvula. Desafortunadamente, no hay mucho material disponible en el válvula "
"de flotador que permita un aumento significativo del diámetro del pasador."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:177
msgid ""
"The maximum coagulant stock concentrations had been 120 g/L as granular PACl"
" prior to the plant at Gracias, Honduras. At Gracias the coagulant stock "
"concentration was 150 g/L of granular PACl. As the concentration of PACl "
"increases it becomes more difficult to mix, the viscosity of the solution "
"increases, and the rate of incrustation of the float valve and dosing tubes "
"increases."
msgstr ""
"Las concentraciones máximas de stock de coagulante habían sido de 120 g/L "
"como PACl granular antes de la planta de Gracias, Honduras. En Gracias, la "
"concentración de stock de coagulante era de 150 g/L de PACl granular. A "
"medida que aumenta la concentración de PACl, se vuelve más difícil "
"mezclarla, la viscosidad de la solución aumenta y la tasa de incrustación "
"del válvula de flotador y los tubos de dosificación."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:179
msgid ""
"At Gracias with 11 g/L of calcium hypochlorite and 150 g/L of granular PACl "
"the operators need to disassemble and clean the dosing systems for both "
"chlorine and PACl once per week. At other AguaClara plants the maintenance "
"interval varies between 2 and 4 weeks. Maintenance for the chlorine system "
"includes removal of the float valve and the dosing tubes and then cleaning "
"those with vinegar to dissolve the deposition of calcium carbonate. The "
"scaling that forms from polyaluminum chloride is water soluble and can be "
"removed with water."
msgstr ""
"En Gracias, con 11 g/L de hipoclorito de calcio y 150 g/L de PACl granular, "
"los operadores deben desmontar y limpiar los sistemas de dosificación tanto "
"de cloro como de PACl una vez por semana. En otras plantas de AguaClara, el "
"intervalo de mantenimiento varía entre 2 y 4 semanas. El mantenimiento del "
"sistema de cloro incluye la retirada del válvula de flotador y los tubos de "
"dosificación y luego la limpieza de estos con vinagre para disolver la "
"deposición de carbonato de calcio. El desincrustado que se forma a partir "
"del cloruro de polialuminio es soluble en agua y puede eliminarse con agua."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:181
msgid ""
"The dosing systems should either be designed to be cleaned with vinegar in "
"place or to be easily disassembled and cleaned. Given the relatively large "
"volume of 1/2\" diameter PVC piping that connects the components of the "
"system the preferred option thus far has been to remove the dosing tubes and"
" the float valves for cleaning. We have used barbed fittings for the dosing "
"tubes, but it is quite challenging to remove tubing from barbed fittings and"
" the result has been premature failure of those fittings. For future "
"chemical dosing systems our goal is to use an easy to disconnect coupling "
"that doesn't require taking the tubing off of the barbed fittings for "
"cleaning."
msgstr ""
"Los sistemas de dosificación deben estar diseñados para limpiarse con "
"vinagre en el lugar o para ser fácilmente desmontados y limpiados. Dado el "
"volumen relativamente grande de tubería de PVC de 1/2\" de diámetro que "
"conecta los componentes del sistema, la opción preferida hasta ahora ha sido"
" retirar los tubos de dosificación y las válvulas de flotación para la "
"limpieza. Hemos usado conexiones con púas para los tubos de dosificación, "
"pero es bastante difícil quitar las tuberías de las conexiones con púas y el"
" resultado ha sido un fallo prematuro de esas conexiones. Para futuros "
"sistemas de dosificación química, nuestro objetivo es usar un acoplamiento "
"fácil de desconectar que no requiera quitar el tubo de las conexiones con "
"púas para su limpieza."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:184
msgid "Main Tube diameter"
msgstr "Diámetro del tubo principal"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:186
msgid ""
"The flexible tubing that transports a chemical feed from the dosing tubes to"
" the chemical dose controller and for the coagulant, from the chemical dose "
"controller to the injection port, must be large enough in diameter so that "
"the head loss is very small compared with the head loss of the LFOM. Both "
"major and minor losses may be significant for these chemical pipes because "
"the tubes are relatively long (high L/d ratio) and entrance, exit, and "
"geometry changes in fittings will contribute to minor losses. The tubing "
"diameter can be selected based on the chemical that requires the largest "
"tubing diameter to reduce the number of different types of fitting and "
"tubing required by the water treatment plant."
msgstr ""
"El tubo flexible que transporta una alimentación química desde los tubos de "
"dosificación hasta el controlador de dosis químico y, para el coagulante, "
"desde el controlador químico hasta el puerto de inyección, debe tener un "
"diámetro lo suficientemente grande como para que el pérdida de carga sea muy"
" pequeño en comparación con el pérdida de carga del LFOM. Tanto las pérdidas"
" mayores como las menores pueden ser significativas para estas tuberías "
"químicas porque los tubos son relativamente largos (alta relación L/D) y los"
" cambios en la entrada, salida y geometría de los accesorios contribuyen a "
"pérdidas menores. El diámetro del tubo puede seleccionarse en función del "
"químico que requiere el mayor diámetro para reducir el número de tipos "
"diferentes de conexiones y tubos requeridos por la planta tratamiento de "
"agua ."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:192
msgid "Summary"
msgstr "Resumen"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:194
msgid ""
"**LFOM:** The LFOM makes the water level in the entrance tank linear with "
"respect to the flow out of the entrance tank. This is useful in measuring "
"the flow and is a critical component in AguaClara’s chemical dosing system. "
"The LFOM *measures* the flow through the plant, it does not *control* the "
"flow through the plant."
msgstr ""
"**LFOM:** El LFOM hace que el nivel del agua en el tanque de entrada lineal "
"respecto al flujo que sale del tanque de entrada. Esto es útil para medir el"
" caudal y es un componente crítico en el sistema de dosificación de químicos"
" de AguaClara. El LFOM *mide* el caudal a través de la planta, no *controla*"
" el flujo a través de la planta."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:196
msgid ""
"**The Linear Chemical Dose Controller (CDC)** combines the: * linear "
"relationship between water level and flow in the entrance tank caused by the"
" LFOM, * linear relationship between elevation difference and flow caused by"
" the Hagen-Poiseuille equation, which is only valid for major losses under "
"laminar flow, and * a lever to link the two linear relationships"
msgstr ""
"**El Controlador Lineal de Dosis Química (CDC)** combina la: * relación "
"lineal entre nivel del agua y flujo en el tanque de entrada causada por el "
"LFOM, * relación lineal entre la diferencia de elevación y el flujo causada "
"por la ecuación de Hagen-Poiseuille, que solo es válida para pérdidas "
"importantes bajo flujo laminar, y * una palanca para enlazar las dos "
"relaciones lineales"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Design.rst:201
msgid ""
"To keep the chemical dose constant by automatically adjusting the addition "
"of coagulant and chlorine as the plant flow rate varies. Two sliders on the "
"lever allows the operator to change the dose of coagulant and chlorine "
"independently of the plant flow rate."
msgstr ""
"Para mantener la dosis química constante ajustando automáticamente la "
"adición de coagulante y cloro según varía la caudal de la planta. Dos "
"deslizadores en la palanca permiten al operador cambiar la dosis de "
"coagulante y cloro independientemente de la planta caudal."

